is unknown$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [basic.scope.param]/1: a function parameter's scope begins at its
declaration and includes the rest of the parameter-declaration-clause, so a
later parameter's type may be spelled `decltype(f(orig_iter))' where
`orig_iter' is an earlier parameter (an unevaluated operand,
[expr.prim.id.unqual]).  The front end resolves the parameter list before
the earlier parameters are in scope: "symbol 'orig_iter' is unknown", and
the enclosing function template's body is dropped.  This is libc++'s
`__unwrap_range_impl<Iter, Iter>::__rewrap(Iter __orig_iter,
decltype(std::__unwrap_iter(__orig_iter)) __iter)', reached from every
std::copy / std::equal on pointers (44 `__rewrap_range' drops in the
round-162 audit, residue item 6).
